  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "When **affiliation flexibility** is the priority in a hotel conversion, owners should look first at **soft brands** and **collection brands** that are designed to preserve the property’s existing identity while still plugging into a larger company’s distribution, loyalty, and commercial systems.[1][3][8]\n\nThe main options highlighted in the results include:\n\n- **Marriott**: **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, and **Design Hotels**.[3][6]\n- **Hilton**: **Curio Collection** and **Tapestry Collection**.[2][6][10]\n- **IHG**: **Vignette Collection**.[3]\n- **Hyatt**: **Unbound Collection**.[6]\n- **Choice Hotels**: **Ascend Hotel Collection**.[2][10]\n- **Voluntary soft-brand / consortium options**: **Preferred Hotels & Resorts** and **The Leading Hotels of the World**.[2][10]\n\nFor a conversion specifically, the most attractive brands are usually the ones described as **conversion-oriented** or offering **lighter renovation and design mandates**, because they reduce capex and preserve more of the existing asset.[1][3][10][12] The results also note that some collection models offer **shorter or more flexible contract terms** than traditional franchise structures, which is often a key part of “affiliation flexibility.”[2][13]\n\nIf you want, I can also rank these by **best for minimal capex**, **shortest contract commitment**, or **strongest luxury positioning**.",
